      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the value of $2a+3b$, we substitute the given values of $a$ and $b$ into the expression and simplify step by step.\n\n1. Substitute $a=2-i$ and $b=-1+i$ into the expression $2a+3b$:\n   \\[\n   2a+3b = 2(2-i) + 3(-1+i)\n   \\]\n\n2. Distribute the constants inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   2(2-i) + 3(-1+i) = 2 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot i + 3 \\cdot (-1) + 3 \\cdot i\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplify the expression by combining like terms:\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot i + 3 \\cdot (-1) + 3 \\cdot i = 4 - 2i - 3 + 3i\n   \\]\n\n4. Combine the real and imaginary parts:\n   \\[\n   4 - 3 - 2i + 3i = 1 + i\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $2a+3b$ is $\\boxed{1+i}$.",
